# Manuscript sources live alongside the code but are never part of the release.
# Anchored and capitalised to avoid shadowing the n0vtla/ package on
# case-insensitive filesystems.
# CAUTION: this does NOT actually work on macOS/Windows -- git defaults to
# core.ignorecase=true there, so `/N0VTLA/` silently matches (and hides every NEW,
# not-yet-tracked file under) the real `/n0vtla/` package too. Found 2026-09-07 when a
# freshly-added source file under n0vtla/ was silently missing from `git status` on a Mac
# clone. Un-ignore the real package explicitly until this pattern is renamed to something
# that can't collide (e.g. a directory name that isn't just a case variant of `n0vtla`).
/N0VTLA/
!/n0vtla/

# data / assets (norm stats are computed per-dataset, provided out-of-band)
# Anchored to the repo root so source packages like src/n0vtla/models/ stay tracked.
/data/
/datasets/
# `/assets/*` (not `/assets/`) deliberately: a plain directory-exclude prunes git's
# traversal entirely, so a negation for anything below it is silently ineffective --
# the wildcard excludes each top-level entry individually instead, which negation CAN
# override. Exception: a small, self-contained, committed normalization manifest (no
# real data, just normal_baseline/normal_scale/task_scale float tables) shipped as a
# Docker asset for train_stage1.sh's default VTLA_ITW_NORMALIZATION -- distinct from
# the runtime-generated `assets/<config.name>/<asset_id>/...` trees this rule protects.
/assets/*
!/assets/itw_normalization/
/pretrained/
/models/
/outputs/
/artifacts/

# Internal cluster runbook: names live pools, queues, CFS instances, load balancers and
# bastion hosts. Keep it in the internal docs vault, never in this repository.
/aihc/

# OS
.DS_Store
